Well, I deserved it.  I'm still upset though.  In four years of
playing nethack I have never made it very far.  The rogue level and
the Norn for the Valkyrie is about as far as I've ever made it.  I
thought the way things were going in this game I'd at least get to the
quest.  But fate knew otherwise...

I was doing insanely well from dungeon level 1.  If I were a more
experienced nethack player, that probably would have made me worried,
but nah, I was having too much fun.  While the chances I were taking
were embarrassing (I did manage to put on an amulet of changing,
slapping a set of balls onto my Valk) I hit pay dirt in the form of a
fountain(1).  Quaffing a fountain had summon a water demon that
granted me a wish (what luck!), so I wished for a grey dragon scale
mail, put it on and proceeded to blast through sokoban, then the
mines, like I was on crack.  Found a golden naga hatchling in the
mines that granted me poison resistance.  Once that happened I thought
there'd be no stoppin' me(2).

I found an amulet of ESP and a ring of slow digestion. I made it to
mines end and found the luck stone.  I had numerous pet cats and dogs.
I had a ton of wands, scrolls and potions. I hadn't ID'ed most of it
yet, but none of them were cursed.  Everything was looking up.  I
hadn't found a pair a gloves yet.  No big deal, I thought...

I couldn't remember if I'd managed to eat a floating eye corpse and
since I had an amulet of ESP but no towel or blindfold, I hadn't been
paying close attention.  So after coming back up from finding the luck
stone I decided to pay one of the merchant's a visit in mine town.  On
the way a nice bold-yellow "c" decided to pay me a visit.  Check
inventory, hmmm, lizard corpse...check, armor...check, shoes...check,
gloves...darn looks like I won't be wielding the rubber chicken
anytime soon.  Time to die Mr. c.  Squish!  One less beasty to worry
about.  I nonchalantly marched my way over the poor creature's corpse
and headed to a store where I managed to find a nice blindfold which I
purchased.  I then proceeded to put it on and take off the amulet.
Rats!  Looks like I haven't managed to feast on a floating eye corpse
after all, let me put that amulet back on.  I think I'll keep this
blindfold on since I can telepathically sense everybody but the
undead, plants, and slimy things.  And all those things are wimpy
anyway, 'cept maybe those ettin mummies.  La de da, de do, guess I'll
stroll along mine town for a bit, oh, golly gee!  There's something on
the ground here, what could it be?  Let's feel and see!

So a statue of my gender changed valk is sitting in mine town, bent
over with her (his?) ass crack showing, with a blind fold on, waiting
to moon countless generations of adventurers.  If I ever come across
the bones I swear I'm gonna kick her (him?) in the ass.

After having my equipment ID'ed turns out I had a ring of free action
too.  Daaaaaaaaamn.  That game would have gone so well....

Still...farthest I've ever gotten without getting an artifact and
being illiterate.  Oh well, lessons learned...

[1] I have a tendency to do crazy things in the first three levels of
the dungeon because I figure that if it gets me killed I haven't
wasted much time and if it pays off, the rest of the game goes really
smoothly.

[2] Incidentally I'd had my last Valk get iced by a fatally poisoned
mordor orc arrow around Dlvl 4, so I was particularly happy about this
turn of events.  Especially after falling on a poisoned spiked pit a
few turns later.

